  "note": "Lean proves Ramaré's Lemma 3.4 for all d (with 7.04 internally), which contains both lines; it is not one of the hypotheses. Erratum: The product prod_p(1 + (p^{1/3} + p^{2/3})/(p(p-1))) that [Ram95] (3.9) bounds by 8 already passes 8 at p = 14629 and is 8.0723 for p <= 2*10^6, so 0.9105 times it exceeds 7.35, not 7.284; the script checks only this numerical content, not the text of Ramare's proof. c_E = 1.3325822757332 lies outside the printed 1.332582275 + O*(10^-9/3). (checked by `scripts/checks/eq_c_10.py`)."
